<newsitem itemid="405172" id="root" date="1997-02-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Vardon Plc 96 profit rises 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Vardon Plc 96 profit rises 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.8		    vs 7.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.45		   vs 1.25</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 1.9		    vs 1.65</p>
<p> Pretax		    11.8		    vs 9.1</p>
<p> Turnover		  77.4		    vs 52.6</p>
<p>Full company name - Vardon Plc.</p>
<p>NOTE -  Leisure group Vardon said it looked forward to 1997 with &quot;considerable confidence&quot;. It said its move into health and fitness reduced the importance of the summer months and that it looked to deliver one third of profits in the first half.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
